post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

To set the PSK file for the system fprintd service, run this command:
sudo install -d -m 755 /etc/systemd/system/fprintd.service.d && printf '%s\n' '[Service]' 'Environment=GOODIX_5F10_PSK_FILE=/var/lib/fprint/goodix-5f10/psk' | sudo tee /etc/systemd/system/fprintd.service.d/goodix-5f10.conf >/dev/null && sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl restart fprintd

The package includes the public author PSK at
/var/lib/fprint/goodix-5f10/psk-default. This fallback works only if the sensor
has already been provisioned with that key; package installation does not
change the sensor. A recovered per-device PSK at /var/lib/fprint/goodix-5f10/psk
takes precedence. Store it as root:root with mode 0600. For example:
sudo install -D -o root -g root -m 600 /path/to/recovered/psk /var/lib/fprint/goodix-5f10/psk

Each file must contain exactly 32 raw bytes, not hexadecimal text. The driver
uses /var/lib/fprint/goodix-5f10/psk by default and falls back to psk-default
only when that preferred file is absent. The systemd override is optional unless
you use a different path.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}
